//! run
//! flags: -I ../../src/fort -I support
//! stdout:
//| ok
import lifetime;

// The `--tokens` mode of the driver gives back everything it takes. That mode
// holds a session and a token vector.
// D20.5
//
// support/lifetime.ft states the rule of the probe, the two views and the
// size of a round. This file is one of six, one for each mode of the driver,
// because the harness kills a program at 60 s (toolchain.md 7.3) and the six
// modes in one program passed alone and timed out under load.
// T-094: one probe for each mode of the driver
//
// Verified by deletion, one release at a time, each one moving a view past
// lifetime.BOUND and turning this test red: the `defer session.free(&s)`, the
// `defer lexer.tokvec_free(&toks)` and the `defer strbuf.free(&dump)` of
// driver.tokens_entry. This test is the only witness of all three.
// Every release of the six modes was measured this way, one deletion at a
// time, against all six tests. The count of the releases of the six modes,
// the command that measures them and the one release that no single test
// witnesses stand in support/lifetime.ft, once for the six tests.
// T-094: one probe for each mode of the driver
fn i32 main() {
    lifetime.write_runtime();
    lifetime.write_file("clean.ft", "fn i32 main() {\n    return 0;\n}\n");
    string[3] mut tokens = {"fort", "--tokens", "clean.ft"};
    assert(lifetime.measure(tokens[0..3]) < lifetime.BOUND);
    println("ok");
    return 0;
}
